WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.640
Today we meet some wonderful Russian animal words that will help you talk about the creatures all around us, from tiny birds to big bears. I'm Olia, and this is привет, Русский, episode 67. Our word of the day is pinguine, pinguine. It sounds like p-e-ng-win. This word means pinguine. Imagine a pinguine waddling like a little black and white tuxedo bird. Repeat after me, pinguine. Here is a simple sentence

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:46.280
with our word. Pinguine plava it in water. The pinguine swims in the water. You can picture the black and white bird moving through the ocean waves using this exact phrase. The transliteration p-e-ng-win helps English speakers say it correctly on the first try.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:58.320
Listeners often find the memory hook of a tuxedo bird makes the meaning easy to recall during practice. Now let's build more vocabulary with animals you might see in stories or at the zoo.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:22.040
Remember Karova from a few lessons ago. It means Karova, and means Karova, the Karova, gives milk. This review word connects to the sound it makes when spoken slowly. The example shows how the animal provides something useful every day. You can repeat the full sentence to practice both the noun and the action it performs.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:38.860
Next comes Ptitsa. Ptitsa. It sounds like p-t-e-e-t-sa. This word means bird. Ptitsa летает в небе, the bird flies in the sky. The memory hook that links it to the English word twit fits the way birds communicate.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:48.280
Speakers use this term for any feathered creature moving overhead. Repeating the sentence helps lock in both the pronunciation and the action described.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:02:07.980
Рыба comes next. Рыба. It sounds like R-Y-B-A. This word means fish. Рыба плавает в озере. The fish swims in the lake. The shorter sound similar to river reminds learners that fish belong in water. The example sentence places the animal in a calm body of water.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:28.880
Practicing the transliteration R-Y-B-A builds confidence with the soft ending sound. Заяц sounds bouncy, just like the animal itself. Заяц. Заяц. This word means hair. Заяц прыгает быстро. The hair jumps quickly. The memory hook highlights the lively motion that matches the words' rhythm.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:38.380
The sentence focuses on speed as the key trait of this animal. Listeners can say the phrase loud to fill the energetic quality in the pronunciation.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:53.120
Волк is our next animal. Волк. It sounds like Волк. This word means wolf. Волк живет в лесу. The wolf lives in the forest. The memory hook connects it to the idea of a folk group that stays together.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:03:01.680
The example shows the animal's natural home among trees. Repeating the full sentence reinforces the location and the noun together.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:14.780
Медведь follows right after. Медведь. It sounds like медвьет. This word means bear. Медведь есть мед. The bear eats honey. The memory hook explains that мед means honey.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:27.860
So the full word describes the one who knows where to find it. The sentence gives a clear action the animal performs. The transliteration медведь captures the stress on the second syllable for accurate speech.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:37.420
Собака is a friendly one. Собака. It sounds like Собака. This word means dog. Собака бежит быстро. The dog runs fast.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:45.920
The memory hook of Собака. Matches the sound dogs make. The example highlights movement as a common dog behavior.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:04:00.080
Practicing the sentence helps combine the noun with a simple verb. Кошка closes our list for today. Кошка. It sounds like Кошка. This word means cat. Кошка спит на окне. The cat slips on the window.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:12.740
The memory hook describes the cozy curled up position cats often take. The sentence places the animal in a common indoor spot. Repeating the phrase builds familiarity with the soft ending sound.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:23.880
Рашин nouns have three genders. Most animal words ending in a consonant are masculine like vulc. Words ending in A are usually feminine like корова.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:35.120
Look at these examples. Волк большой. The wolf is big. That ending shows masculine. Корова большая. The cow is big. That ending shows feminine.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:44.480
This is different from English, where adjectives stay the same. The pattern appears clearly when the same adjective changes its ending to match the noun.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:59.180
Let me share something really cool about one of today's words. The word mid-wet started long ago in Slavic languages as a polite nickname. People once feared the real name of the bear, so they called it the one who knows honey.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:09.940
Мед means honey, and ved means knover. English bear comes from a completely different root, that means brown. That makes it a fun-falls friend in sound and meaning.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:24.520
Picture a bear sniffing out honey like a detective who always finds the sweet stuff. That picture helps the word stick. The breakdown into two clear parts gives learners a reliable way to remember the origin each time they say it.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:35.480
In Russian fairy tales, the bear often appears as a strong but kind forest character. Stories like Masha and the bear show the bear as big, a little clumsy and friendly.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:41.020
The animal lives in the woods and interacts with the main hero in helpful or tasting ways.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:51.560
Listeners recognize this figure from traditional tales passed down through generations. The description feeds the gentle yet powerful image Russians associate with the word.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:06:07.960
For kids, draw your favorite animal and say it's Russian name out loud three times while you color. For adults, look around your home or neighborhood, point to any animal even in a picture and say the Russian word in a sentence like это собака, молодец.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:18.760
That means well done. Remember every expert started as a beginner. Practice saying today's words out loud even just once and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

